+For each material path, return one compact evidence row or equivalent prose:
+
+| Path / requirement | Input and actual validator | Result producer / shared data | Consumer and resulting state | Code / planned check / verdict |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+
+Follow a changed value through the consumer's subsequent update, rendering or
+persistence step, not just to receipt of the response. Check whether the data
+supplied is sufficient for that consumer and whether later logic keeps, clears
+or replaces the promised result. Distinct validators and early returns need
+their own evidence when they change the outcome. Verify that planned commands
+select the claimed checks. Record material paths not inspected or not settled
+as `unknown`, including a missing product decision; do not omit them from the
+aggregate R1–R5 verdict. Keep this proportional to changed contracts, not every
+function or a Cartesian product of cases. A missing shared contract is a finding;
+an unspecified private helper is not. Review the retained approval text as well
+as the documents, including every optional graph edge. When independent review
+is unavailable or unwarranted, the coordinator uses the same path evidence.
